<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>HHF Blog Data</title>
<style>body{font:16px/1.5 system-ui,sans-serif;max-width:46rem;margin:0 auto;padding:1rem}code{background:#8882;padding:.1em .3em}</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>HHF threat data</h1>
<p>Structured data behind the daily threat briefings on <a href="{{ blog_url }}">the HHF blog</a>. {{ n_briefings }} briefings, {{ n_cves }} CVEs. Generated {{ m.generated }}.</p>
<p><strong>Disclaimer.</strong> {{ m.disclaimer }}</p>
<h2>Endpoints</h2>
<ul>
<li><a href="{{ pages_url }}/api/v1/briefings.json"><code>/api/v1/briefings.json</code></a> last 30 briefings</li>
<li><a href="{{ pages_url }}/api/v1/cves/latest.json"><code>/api/v1/cves/latest.json</code></a> CVEs updated in the last 7 days</li>
<li><a href="{{ pages_url }}/api/v1/cves.json"><code>/api/v1/cves.json</code></a> all CVEs</li>
<li><a href="{{ pages_url }}/feed.xml"><code>/feed.xml</code></a> RSS 2.0</li>
<li><code>/cve/&lt;id&gt;.html</code> one page per CVE</li>
</ul>
<h2>Licence</h2>
<p>The structured data (JSON files and CVE pages) is licensed <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">{{ m.license }}</a>: {{ m.licenseScope }}. The article prose is copyright HHF Technology and is not licensed for reuse. Code: MIT, see the <a href="{{ m.source }}">source repository</a>.</p>
<h2>Attribution</h2>
<ul>
{% for a in m.attribution %}
<li>{{ a }}</li>
{% endfor %}
</ul>
</body>
</html>
